# KindBridge architecture rules

Product name is **KindBridge** (not AidSync). Before writing code, read the relevant specs in `docs/` (`system-spec.md`, `architecture.md`, `event-sourcing.md`, `agent-and-mcp.md`). If code and specs disagree, the specs win; update them first.

## CQRS

Mutating routes dispatch a Command through `app/commands/bus.py`. GET routes dispatch a Query handler from `app/queries/`. Queries never append to `event_store` or mutate projections.

## Event Sourcing

Immutable events include `event_id`, `aggregate_id`, `aggregate_type`, `event_type`, `payload_json`, `version`, `created_at`. Optimistic concurrency on `version` yields HTTP 409. Projections are rebuildable. Never put plaintext passwords in event payloads. Never log passwords or hashes.

## Layering

No SQL or business rules in controllers. `app/domain` must not import Flask, SQL, or Chroma. SQL only via repository interfaces, so SQL Server can be swapped for LocalDB in tests. Chroma and embeddings only via `app/infrastructure`. One command/query file per aggregate.

## Agent

Separate process: `python -m agent.main`. Writes only via `ProposeMatchCommand` on the same command bus. Never approves or assigns.

## Tests

Every new endpoint ships a happy-path test and a 401/403 test. Agent tests mock MCP and Chroma.

## Secrets

Env vars only. Never commit `.env`.
